    "q": "<p>Using the indirect method, the cash flows for the movement of the working capital are:</p><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><div><span>£100,000 cash inflow for inventories, £10,000 cash outflow for trade receivables, £50,000 cash outflow for trade and other payables</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><div><span>£100,000 cash outflow for inventories, £10,000 cash outflow for trade receivables, £50,000 cash outflow for trade and other payables</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">c)</span><div><span>£100,000 cash inflow for inventories, £10,000 cash inflow for trade receivables, £50,000 cash outflow for trade and other payables</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">d)</span><div><span>£100,000 cash outflow for inventories, £10,000 cash inflow for trade receivables, £50,000 cash inflow for trade and other payables</span></div></div>",
    "a": "<p class=\"answer-key\">The correct answer is b.</p><p>Working capital movements</p><p>Inventories</p><p>Trade receivables</p><p>Trade and other payables</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><caption><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span></caption><tbody><tr><td>Opening</td><td class=\"num\">900</td><td class=\"num\">540</td><td class=\"num\">500</td></tr><tr><td>Closing</td><td class=\"num\">1,000</td><td class=\"num\">550</td><td class=\"num\">450</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Increase/</p><p>(decrease)</p><p>100</p><p>10</p><p>(50)</p>",
