    "lesson": "Lesson1",
    "appendix": {
      "title": "Case information",
      "html": "<p>You are the financial controller of M Ltd (M) and today you must prepare the statement of cash flows, in accordance with IFRS® Accounting Standards. M uses the indirect method for preparing cash generated from operations.</p><p>To finance its future business ventures, M issued 200,000 £1 ordinary shares during the year for a cash consideration of £2 per share. Expenses were £50,000 and M opted to write these off to share premium.</p><p>Further, M obtained new loans of £600,000 during the year. All loans are classified as amortised cost. Effective and nominal interest on all loans is equal and was £120,000 for the year. Finally, the firm issued 250,000 £1 10% debentures at par on 1 January 20X3. Debentures all have a £1 par value and are classified as amortised cost, with effective and nominal interest of 10%. All interest due in the year was paid.</p><p>In terms of asset development, M entered into a lease agreement on 31 December 20X3 and obtained a right-of-use asset of £55,000 that was recognised on that date. The first payment is due in more than 12 months from the year end. The corresponding lease payable was accounted for correctly. Right-of-use assets are presented within property, plant and equipment (PPE).</p><p>There was also a revaluation of properties during the year. A net revaluation increase of £120,350 was recognised. This was net of deferred tax, at 17%, of £24,650. M does not make annual transfers from the revaluation surplus to retained earnings. It should also be noted that the depreciation charge for the year was £300,000, while the short-term investments are insignificant investments in equity and are not cash equivalents. There was no change in the fair value of any of the short-term investments during the year. No dividends were received on these investments during the year.</p><p>Since it was a profitable year for the firm, M declared and paid dividends equal to £48,000 during the year. Finally, due to tax losses carried forward and utilised, no tax was paid in 20X3.</p><p>The statement of profit or loss and the statement of financial position are provided below.</p><p>Statement of financial position</p><p>M Ltd</p><p>Statement of financial position</p><p>For the year ended 31 December 20X3</p><p>20X3</p><p>20X2</p><p>£’000</p><p>£’000</p><p>ASSETS</p><p>Non-current assets</p><p>Property, plant and equipment</p><p>5,000</p><p>3,000</p><p>5,000</p><p>3,000</p><p>Current assets</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Inventories</td><td class=\"num\">1,000</td><td class=\"num\">900</td><td class=\"num\"></td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Trade receivables</td><td class=\"num\">550</td><td class=\"num\">540</td><td class=\"num\"></td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Investments</td><td class=\"num\">150</td><td class=\"num\">60</td><td class=\"num\"></td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Cash and cash equivalents</td><td class=\"num\">725</td><td class=\"num\">500</td><td class=\"num\">2,425</td><td class=\"num\">2,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total assets</td><td class=\"num\">7,425</td><td class=\"num\">5,000</td><td class=\"num\"></td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>EQUITY AND LIABILITIES</p><p>Equity</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Share capital</td><td class=\"num\">1,200</td><td class=\"num\">1,000</td></tr><tr><td>Share premium</td><td class=\"num\">400</td><td class=\"num\">250</td></tr><tr><td>Revaluation surplus</td><td class=\"num\">120</td><td class=\"num\">-</td></tr><tr><td>Retained earnings</td><td class=\"num\">1,025</td><td class=\"num\">150</td></tr><tr><td>Total equity</td><td class=\"num\">2,745</td><td class=\"num\">1,400</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Non-current liabilities</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Debentures</td><td class=\"num\">1,250</td><td class=\"num\">1,000</td></tr><tr><td>Loans payable</td><td class=\"num\">1,950</td><td class=\"num\">1,600</td></tr><tr><td>Deferred tax</td><td class=\"num\">25</td><td class=\"num\">-</td></tr><tr><td>Lease payable</td><td class=\"num\">55</td><td class=\"num\">-</td></tr><tr><td>Total non-current liabilities</td><td class=\"num\">3,280</td><td class=\"num\">2,600</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Current liabilities</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Bank overdrafts</td><td class=\"num\">750</td><td class=\"num\">400</td></tr><tr><td>Trade and other payables</td><td class=\"num\">450</td><td class=\"num\">500</td></tr><tr><td>Loans payable</td><td class=\"num\">200</td><td class=\"num\">100</td></tr><tr><td>Total current liabilities</td><td class=\"num\">1,400</td><td class=\"num\">1,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total liabilities</td><td class=\"num\">4,680</td><td class=\"num\">3,600</td></tr><tr><td>Total equity and liabilities</td><td class=\"num\">7,425</td><td class=\"num\">5,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Statement of profit or loss</p><p>M Ltd</p><p>Statement of profit or loss</p><p>For the year ended 31 December 20X3</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><caption><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span></caption><tbody><tr><td>Revenue</td><td class=\"num\">8,100</td></tr><tr><td>Cost of sales</td><td class=\"num\">(5,600)</td></tr><tr><td>Gross profit</td><td class=\"num\">2,500</td></tr><tr><td>General and administrative expenses</td><td class=\"num\">(1,362)</td></tr><tr><td>Operating profit</td><td class=\"num\">1,138</td></tr><tr><td>Interest income</td><td class=\"num\">30</td></tr><tr><td>Profit before financing and incomes taxes</td><td class=\"num\">1,168</td></tr><tr><td>Interest expense</td><td class=\"num\">(245)</td></tr><tr><td>Profit before incomes taxes</td><td class=\"num\">923</td></tr><tr><td>Income tax expense</td><td class=\"num\">0</td></tr><tr><td>PROFIT FOR THE PERIOD</td><td class=\"num\">923</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
    },
