    "q": "<p>The net cash from financing activities is equal to:</p><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><div><span>£350,000</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><div><span>£757,000</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">c)</span><div><span>£1,002,000</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">d)</span><div><span>£2,150,000</span></div></div>",
    "a": "<p class=\"answer-key\">The correct answer is b.</p><p>Interest paid</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><caption><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span></caption><tbody><tr><td>Debentures (10% x £1,250)</td><td class=\"num\">125</td></tr><tr><td>Loans</td><td class=\"num\">120</td></tr><tr><td>Interest paid</td><td class=\"num\">245</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Proceeds from issue of share capital (£’000)</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><caption><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span></caption><tbody><tr><td>Gross proceeds (200 x £2)</td><td class=\"num\">400</td></tr><tr><td>Issue costs</td><td class=\"num\">(50)</td></tr><tr><td>Proceeds from issue of share capital</td><td class=\"num\">350</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Alternative workings on the proceeds from issue of share capital</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Opening share capital and premium (1,000 + 250)</td><td class=\"num\">1,250</td></tr><tr><td>Closing share capital and premium (1,200 + 400)</td><td class=\"num\">1,600</td></tr><tr><td>Proceeds from issue of share capital</td><td class=\"num\">350</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Payment of long-term borrowings</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Opening loans payable (£1,600 + £100)</td><td class=\"num\">1,700</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Proceeds from issue of long-term borrowings</td><td class=\"num\">600</td><td class=\"num\">2,300</td></tr><tr><td>Closing loans payable (£1,950 + £200)</td><td class=\"num\">2,150</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Payment of long-term borrowings</td><td class=\"num\">150</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Cash flows from financing activities</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><caption><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span></caption><tbody><tr><td>Proceeds from issue of share capital</td><td class=\"num\">350</td></tr><tr><td>Proceeds from issue of loan obtained</td><td class=\"num\">600</td></tr><tr><td>Proceeds from long-term borrowings</td><td class=\"num\">250</td></tr><tr><td>Payment of long-term borrowings</td><td class=\"num\">(150)</td></tr><tr><td>Interest paid</td><td class=\"num\">(245)</td></tr><tr><td>Dividends paid</td><td class=\"num\">(48)</td></tr><tr><td>Net cash from financing activities</td><td class=\"num\">757</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>As an illustration, the full statement of cash flows would be as follows:</p><p>M Ltd</p><p>Statement of cash flows</p><p>For the year ended 31 December 20X3</p><p>£’000</p><p>£’000</p><p>Cash flows from operating activities</p><p>Operating profit</p><p>1,138</p><p>Adjustments for:</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Depreciation charge</td><td class=\"num\">300</td><td class=\"num\">1,438</td></tr><tr><td>Increase in inventories</td><td class=\"num\">(100)</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Increase in trade receivables</td><td class=\"num\">(10)</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Decrease in trade and other payables</td><td class=\"num\">(50)</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Cash from operating activities before income taxes</td><td class=\"num\">1,278</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Net cash from operating activities</td><td class=\"num\">1,278</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Cash flows from investing activities</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Purchase of property, plant and equipment</td><td class=\"num\">(2,100)</td></tr><tr><td>Purchase of investments</td><td class=\"num\">(90)</td></tr><tr><td>Interest received</td><td class=\"num\">30</td></tr><tr><td>Net cash used in investing activities</td><td class=\"num\">(2,160)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Cash flows from financing activities</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Proceeds from issue of share capital</td><td class=\"num\">350</td></tr><tr><td>Proceeds from issue of loan obtained</td><td class=\"num\">250</td></tr><tr><td>Proceeds from long-term borrowings</td><td class=\"num\">600</td></tr><tr><td>Payment of long-term borrowings</td><td class=\"num\">(150)</td></tr><tr><td>Interest paid</td><td class=\"num\">(245)</td></tr><tr><td>Dividends paid</td><td class=\"num\">(48)</td></tr><tr><td>Net cash from financing activities</td><td class=\"num\">757</td></tr><tr><td>Net decrease in cash and cash equivalents</td><td class=\"num\">(125)</td></tr><tr><td>Cash and cash equivalents at 1 January 20X3</td><td class=\"num\">100</td></tr><tr><td>Cash and cash equivalents at 31 December 20X3</td><td class=\"num\">(25)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>20X3</p><p>20X2</p><p>£’000</p><p>£’000</p><p>Cash and cash equivalents</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Cash and cash equivalents (current assets)</td><td class=\"num\">725</td><td class=\"num\">500</td></tr><tr><td>Bank overdrafts</td><td class=\"num\">(750)</td><td class=\"num\">(400)</td></tr><tr><td>Cash and cash equivalents</td><td class=\"num\">(25)</td><td class=\"num\">100</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
