    "source": "M7 Skills Builder Q11",
    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<p>What is the amount that will be presented as “Proceeds on disposal of subsidiary, net of cash disposed of” in the consolidated statement of cash flows?</p><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><div><span>£1,156,000</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><div><span>£1,680,000</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">c)</span><div><span>£2,350,000</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">d)</span><div><span>£2,500,000</span></div></div>",
    "a": "<p class=\"answer-key\">The correct answer is c.</p><p>The amount that will be disclosed as “Proceeds on disposal of subsidiary, net of cash disposed of” in the consolidated statement of cash flows is equal with the amount of consideration received (£2,500,000) minus the cash of the disposed company (£150,000).</p>",
    "isHTML": true,
    "linkTags": [
      "cash-flows-consolidated"
    ],
    "lesson": "Lesson2",
    "appendix": {
      "title": "Case information",
      "html": "<p>Let’s assume that Foxtrot also holds 80% of Bachata Ltd (Bachata), which is sold for £2,500,000 cash. The stand-alone statement of financial position for Bachata at disposal date is provided below:</p><p>Fair value of net assets disposed of</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><caption><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span></caption><tbody><tr><td>Non-current assets</td><td class=\"num\">1,200</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Inventory</td><td class=\"num\">450</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Trade receivables</td><td class=\"num\">200</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Cash</td><td class=\"num\">150</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Trade payables</td><td class=\"num\">(320)</td><td class=\"num\">1,680</td></tr><tr><td>Ordinary shares £1</td><td class=\"num\">1,000</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Reserves</td><td class=\"num\">680</td><td class=\"num\">1,680</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
    },
